    <item>
      <title>[리뷰] BiRefNet (1회독)</title>
      <link>https://blog.heozeop.kr/post/review-birefnet-1/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 19 Apr 2025 20:06:33 +0900</pubDate>
      <guid>https://blog.heozeop.kr/post/review-birefnet-1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;tldr&#34;&gt;TL;DR&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BiRefNet 논문을 1회 읽어 보았다.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;읽기도 벅찼다.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;다음에 읽을게 많다.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;birefnet&#34;&gt;BiRefNet&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;정보&#34;&gt;정보&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;논문 제목: Bilateral Reference for High-Resolution Dichotomous Image Segmentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;저자: Peng Zheng, Dehong Gao, Deng-Ping Fan, Li Liu, Jorma Laaksonen, Wanli Ouyang, Nicu Sebe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;링크: &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/pdf/2401.03407&#34;&gt;https://arxiv.org/pdf/2401.03407&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;목적&#34;&gt;목적&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;고해상도 이진 이미지 분할(DIS, Dichotomous Image Segmentation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;기존 모델(&lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.14482&#34; title=&#34;High Quality Segmentation for Ultra High-resolution Images&#34;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/4767837&#34; title=&#34;A Pyramid-Based Approach to Segmentation Applied to Region Matching&#34;&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.08545&#34; title=&#34;ICNet for Real-Time Semantic Segmentation on High-Resolution Images&#34;&gt;3&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.09475&#34; title=&#34;Revisiting Image Pyramid Structure for High Resolution Salient Object Detection&#34;&gt;4&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2023/0124.pdf&#34; title=&#34;Locate, Refine and Restore: A Progressive Enhancement Network for Camouflaged Object Detection&#34;&gt;5&lt;/a&gt;)는 배경과 비슷한 경계 등을 잘 분리하지 못하는 한계가 있었음&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;핵심-아이디어&#34;&gt;핵심 아이디어&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;분리된 localization module과 reconsturction module을 사용해 높은 해상도의 이미지 DIS를 진행한다.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
